WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Nearly 12,000 older adults in a randomized trial had fewer falls and injuries. This is Longevity Weekly Episode 7, the science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. After that, a review of protein and aging, blood proteins tied to mortality, and a closer look at methylation clocks. Medical dialogues describe the advice as personalized and built into primary care, with the change showing up in clinic records of falls and of the injuries that followed them. The write-up does not say how large that drop was.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.401
was, it is a behavior tested in people, not a medicine. University of Wisconsin

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:39.441
medicine researchers, writing in the well news, published a review in

00:00:39.441 --> 00:00:44.821
Cell Press Blue in August 2026 on eating less protein or less of particular

00:00:44.821 --> 00:00:49.681
amino acids while still covering nutritional needs. In yeast, flies, and

00:00:49.681 --> 00:00:53.441
rodents, lower protein diets have lengthened life and improved metabolic

00:00:53.441 --> 00:00:58.481
measures, sometimes without a cut in total calories. Short trials in people

00:00:58.481 --> 00:01:03.921
have reported metabolic changes and the review does not establish regulatory approval of protein

00:01:03.921 --> 00:01:09.981
restriction for any aging-related use. In one of those trials, 43 days of a low protein diet

00:01:09.981 --> 00:01:15.341
brought down body weight, fat, and fasting blood sugar, even though people ate more calories.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:19.721
A separate five-week intervention in lean men improved insulin sensitivity,

00:01:20.321 --> 00:01:23.341
meaning the body answered the blood sugar hormone more effectively.

00:01:24.101 --> 00:01:29.741
fibroblast growth factor 21 rises when protein is restricted, in humans and in rodents.

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:33.101
Whether any of this extends human lifespan is still unknown.

00:01:34.262 --> 00:01:41.022
Fight aging reports a perspective cohort, not a treatment test, that screened 4,265 plasma

00:01:41.022 --> 00:01:45.082
proteins in 1,025 older adults from the long-genity study.

00:01:45.502 --> 00:01:51.782
Over a mean of 8.05 years, 17 proteins were significantly tied to death from any cause,

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:58.102
and those links were checked in 1,124 people in the Baltimore Longitudinal Study of Aging.

00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:04.882
Higher epidermal growth factor receptor, also called ERBB-1, and higher anthrax toxin

00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:11.342
receptor 2, and tex R2, went with lower mortality and a younger proteomic age across several

00:02:11.342 --> 00:02:21.202
organ systems. Higher growth differentiation factor 15, human epididimus protein 4, and

00:02:21.202 --> 00:02:26.862
the other way, more deaths and an older biological age across organ systems. Elevated

00:02:26.862 --> 00:02:32.882
MIC-1 lined up with an older organismal age, while ER-BB-1 lined up with a younger liver

00:02:32.882 --> 00:02:39.022
age. The commentary adds the usual caution. A clock that sorts people by risk may not

00:02:39.022 --> 00:02:44.042
still be measuring biological age if someone later tests an anti-aging intervention against

00:02:44.042 --> 00:02:51.102
it. Science Daily describes a 24-year observational study of more than 8,200 adults in which

00:02:51.102 --> 00:02:56.462
Excess body weight tracked with faster losses of memory, concentration, and decision-making.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:03:02.042
The link was particularly strong after 65, because this follows people rather than

00:03:02.042 --> 00:03:03.542
assigning a weight loss program.

00:03:04.062 --> 00:03:07.182
It does not show that losing weight would undo those declines.

00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:13.376
Masteric University Medical Center, in a paper science daily covers from food and function,

00:03:13.956 --> 00:03:18.896
ran a randomized crossover trial in 31 healthy adults between 60 and 75.

00:03:18.896 --> 00:03:25.036
They ate unsalted, skin-roasted peanuts every day for 16 weeks, and also had a period

00:03:25.036 --> 00:03:25.676
without them.

00:03:26.216 --> 00:03:29.996
It is a small human trial, not an approved treatment for cognitive aging.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:35.516
After the peanut period, insulin responsiveness improved in memory-related parts of the right

00:03:35.516 --> 00:03:41.756
hemisphere, portions of the lingual gyros, the hippocampus, the para-hipocampal gyros, and

00:03:41.756 --> 00:03:43.356
the posterior-singulate gyros.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:49.756
And earlier 2025 study from the same senior author, Peter Joris had found that 16 weeks

00:03:49.756 --> 00:03:57.016
of peanuts raised overall cerebral blood flow by 3.6% and verbal memory by 5.8%.

00:03:57.016 --> 00:04:01.396
The new paper suggests the insulin change may help explain those cognitive results.

00:04:02.016 --> 00:04:04.796
It does not show that peanuts prevent Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:10.860
On October 28th, the open question here was whether partial reprogramming could rejuvenate

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:16.460
a cell without tipping it into pleuripotency, and a cell study covered by fight aging now

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.920
tries to keep that door shut.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:24.400
Researchers used a lipid nanoparticle to deliver a circular RNA that co-expresses OCT4,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:30.660
SOX2, and KLF4 in mesenchymal stem cells without rewriting the genome.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:37.280
Droplet digital PCR aimed at the pleuripotency marker ESRG showed that this delivery alone

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.780
did not turn those cells into induced pluripotent stem cells.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:48.380
In senescent late-passage cells, senescence-associated beta-galactocides activity fell, DNA damage markers

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:54.420
fell, and inflammatory cytokine secretion fell, canonical surface markers and genome stability

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.340
stayed in place.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.580
Proliferation, migration, and the ability to form three lineages came back to a level

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.620
comparable with early-passage cells.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.380
That is a cultured dish.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.140
It does not show the same split or any clinical benefit in animals or in people, and cells

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.020
sitting together in a tissue may still need different exposure.

00:05:13.975 --> 00:05:19.455
A methylation clock is a model that turns chemical marks on DNA into an age number, and

00:05:19.455 --> 00:05:22.715
this week's mechanism is what those numbers can and cannot say.

00:05:23.175 --> 00:05:29.315
In 553 healthy breast samples, a tissue-specific clock called BTEC matched chronological

00:05:29.315 --> 00:05:37.255
age with a correlation of 0.91 and a mean absolute error of 3.0 years, without the data set specific

00:05:37.255 --> 00:05:43.355
corrections classical clocks needed there. The marks sit at CPG sites where a methyl group is

00:05:43.355 --> 00:05:49.975
added to cytosine and the pattern shifts across life. The model is not reading mutations, it waits

00:05:49.975 --> 00:05:55.275
a chosen set of sites so the pattern matches age in a training set, then applies those weights

00:05:55.275 --> 00:05:56.235
to a new sample.

00:05:56.935 --> 00:06:01.855
Hanum's clock and Horvath's were built mainly to predict chronological age, and in breast

00:06:01.855 --> 00:06:03.215
tissue they did that poorly.

00:06:03.795 --> 00:06:07.515
A later systematic review compared those two with Levine and Grim Age.

00:06:08.055 --> 00:06:12.795
The four usually pointed the same direction when exposures and diseases were tested, while

00:06:12.795 --> 00:06:15.155
the size of the association changed with the clock.

00:06:15.755 --> 00:06:22.975
A skin and blood estimator uses 391 CPGs because ordinary clocks were inaccurate in fibroblasts

00:06:22.975 --> 00:06:28.875
and other cells grown outside the body. A saliva panel cut the read out to six CPGs after

00:06:28.875 --> 00:06:35.075
screening array data from 76 Han Chinese donors. Tissue, cell type, and the question being asked

00:06:35.075 --> 00:06:40.335
all change which sites are worth reading. The strongest outcome evidence in this set is not a

00:06:40.335 --> 00:06:47.115
new clock. A 2019 systematic review and meta-analysis of methylation age measured in peripheral samples

00:06:47.115 --> 00:06:51.715
levels, covered 23 articles and 41,607 participants.

00:06:51.975 --> 00:06:57.875
Each 5-year increase in DNA methylation age was associated with an 8-15% higher risk

00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:58.275
of death.

00:06:58.855 --> 00:07:00.675
That pool's observational studies.

00:07:01.115 --> 00:07:04.435
It is not a trial in which someone changed a clock and then lived longer.

00:07:04.955 --> 00:07:10.115
The same review called links to age-related disease and to longevity inconclusive, because

00:07:10.115 --> 00:07:14.935
the studies were few and the designs differed, and it warned that positive publication bias

00:07:14.935 --> 00:07:15.955
has to be considered.

00:07:15.955 --> 00:07:23.955
A 2021 systematic review took in 156 publications, with statistics possible for 57 relationships

00:07:23.955 --> 00:07:27.195
across Hanum, Horvath, Levine, and Grimage.

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:32.555
Higher body mass index, HIV infection, and male sex were associated with acceleration

00:07:32.555 --> 00:07:33.875
of one or more clocks.

00:07:34.635 --> 00:07:40.135
Acceleration was also related to mortality, cardiovascular disease, cancer, and diabetes.

00:07:40.135 --> 00:07:40.335
disease.

00:07:41.295 --> 00:07:45.695
Associations in blood-based clock studies not proof that the methylation pattern causes

00:07:45.695 --> 00:07:46.255
the disease.

00:07:46.855 --> 00:07:51.915
In patient cells, the skin and blood clock picked up epigenetic age acceleration in Hutchinson

00:07:51.915 --> 00:07:57.315
Gilford Progeria fibroblasts, at a magnitude other methylation clocks were not sensitive

00:07:57.315 --> 00:07:58.055
enough to see.

00:07:58.595 --> 00:08:03.635
In culture, the same estimator followed cells as they were grown, and proliferation came

00:08:03.635 --> 00:08:05.875
with a steady rise in epigenetic age.

00:08:05.875 --> 00:08:10.995
The paper says this clock predicts lifespan and relates to many age-related conditions.

00:08:11.515 --> 00:08:15.435
BTEC's stress test is a warning against reading a low number as good news.

00:08:16.075 --> 00:08:20.935
Tumor adjacent breast samples ran 2.3 years younger than chronological age on average.

00:08:21.655 --> 00:08:24.275
Tumor samples ran 14 to 15 years younger.

00:08:24.875 --> 00:08:29.715
The distortion was larger in her two positive and triple negative tumors than in hormone receptor

00:08:29.715 --> 00:08:30.715
positive tumors.

00:08:31.335 --> 00:08:35.515
The authors read that as evidence that breast tumors do not generally show accelerated

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:41.275
epigenetic aging. In an exploratory analysis, extreme deviations scored as

00:08:41.275 --> 00:08:45.875
BTEC epigenetic age acceleration were associated with survival in hormone

00:08:45.875 --> 00:08:50.255
receptor-positive breast cancer. The usual correction for prediction bias,

00:08:50.835 --> 00:08:55.135
residual acceleration, depended on which reference data set was used, and did

00:08:55.135 --> 00:08:59.835
not travel as a general fix. Sites in BTEC were tied to genes including

00:08:59.835 --> 00:09:09.915
Jack 1, TP73, PDGFRA, CCND1, and STAT-5B, and to Wint, Hedgehog, and Urb B signaling,

00:09:10.475 --> 00:09:13.635
a biological neighborhood, not a validated clinical test.

00:09:14.155 --> 00:09:21.135
The six CPG saliva models, robust lasso and support vector regression, missed by 3.240

00:09:21.135 --> 00:09:23.715
and 3.267 years in development.

00:09:23.715 --> 00:09:29.775
They held up on three independent data sets, matched Hannum and Horvath, Beat Levine,

00:09:30.075 --> 00:09:36.415
PEDBE, and Wu, and posted lower errors than 85% of 60 previously published saliva clocks.

00:09:36.955 --> 00:09:42.395
A methods result in forensic and research samples, not a trial of an anti-aging intervention.

00:09:42.975 --> 00:09:46.955
What is not established is whether moving a clock changes how long someone lives,

00:09:47.455 --> 00:09:51.055
or whether they avoid disease. None of these abstracts reports a

00:09:51.055 --> 00:09:56.555
regulator accepting a clock as a clinical aging test, and none names a registered human trial

00:09:56.555 --> 00:09:58.655
of an intervention scored by these clocks.

00:09:59.335 --> 00:10:04.055
Tumor biology can pull a reading younger, so a young number can be a distortion rather

00:10:04.055 --> 00:10:04.755
than a benefit.

00:10:05.715 --> 00:10:10.035
Publication bias and disagreement between clocks on the size of an effect stay open.

00:10:10.715 --> 00:10:15.615
The mortality association is the strongest human signal here, and the meta-analysis that

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:19.775
produced it still calls the broader disease and longevity evidence inconclusive.

00:10:19.775 --> 00:10:25.835
One thing worth knowing is that exercise advice inside ordinary primary care was followed

00:10:25.835 --> 00:10:30.675
by fewer documented falls and injuries, a functional outcome rather than a lab marker

00:10:30.675 --> 00:10:31.195
of aging.

00:10:31.815 --> 00:10:37.675
Short human trials of lower protein intake changed weight, fat, fasting blood sugar, or insulin

00:10:37.675 --> 00:10:40.895
sensitivity, and they do not show a longer human life.

00:10:41.355 --> 00:10:46.155
Plasma proteins that track with death and with proteomic age are observational markers,

00:10:46.155 --> 00:10:50.835
measures, so a younger clock reading is not by itself evidence that a treatment worked.

00:10:51.395 --> 00:10:56.415
Daily peanuts in a small crossover trial changed insulin responsiveness in memory-related

00:10:56.415 --> 00:11:00.275
brain regions, which is a step short of showing protection from dementia.

